------------------------------------------------
| Command | Description                         |
| ------- | ----------------------------------- |
| `i`     | Insert line **before** match/line   |
| `a`     | Append line **after** match/line    |
| `c`     | Change (replace) the entire line    |
| `d`     | Delete line(s)                      |
| `s`     | Substitute text (replace string)    |
| `n`     | Read and display the next line      |
| `e`     | Execute a shell command (GNU `sed`) |
| `p`     | Print line(s)                       |
| `q`     | Quit after a certain line           |
--------------------------------------------------
| Command             | Replaces             |
| ------------------- | -------------------- |
| `sed 's/old/new/'`  | First "old" per line |
| `sed 's/old/new/g'` | All "old"s per line  |
